From: Kristianaaron <25537000+Kristianaaron@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: tegra: p3450: Enable HDMI 5 V with MOD_SLEEP* (PA6)

On the Jetson Nano developer kit carrier (P3449), MOD_SLEEP* (GPIO PA6)
enables VDD_3V3_HDMI. That rail switches on the HDMI connector's 5 V
(APL3552 load switch) and powers the DDC level shifter. NVIDIA's L4T
device tree holds PA6 high from boot.

Mainline describes PA6 only as the enable of VDD_HUB_3V3. Since commit
2428787f1615 ("phy: tegra: xusb: Remove usb3 supply") nothing consumes
that regulator, so the fixed regulator driver requests PA6 low at probe.
Without 5 V on pin 18 the monitor never asserts hot-plug detect and the
DDC bus times out: the connector reads "disconnected" and the EDID is
empty, although forced video modes still show.

Make PA6 the enable of VDD_HDMI_5V0 as well (fixed regulators share
enable GPIOs), so the SOR driver turns it on through hdmi-supply, and
mark both regulators boot-on so the line is not driven low at probe.

Checked on a P3449-B01 kit by driving PA6 high: HPD then reads
connected and the EDID reads over DDC (i2c@7000c700).

Origin: jetson-nano-omarchy, carried in linux-nano.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra210-p3450-0000.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra210-p3450-0000.dts
@@ -1824,6 +1824,14 @@
 		regulator-min-microvolt = <5000000>;
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <5000000>;
 
+		/*
+		 * MOD_SLEEP* (PA6) enables VDD_3V3_HDMI, which switches on the
+		 * HDMI 5 V load switch and powers the DDC level shifter.
+		 */
+		gpio = <&gpio TEGRA_GPIO(A, 6) GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+		regulator-boot-on;
+
 		vin-supply = <&vdd_5v0_sys>;
 	};
 
@@ -1836,6 +1844,7 @@
 
 		gpio = <&gpio TEGRA_GPIO(A, 6) GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		enable-active-high;
+		regulator-boot-on;
 
 		vin-supply = <&vdd_5v0_sys>;
 	};
